    "summary": "I built a single-column tower three storeys tall. Each storey is a north-half hex base, because the configurator only lets a base stack on a base of the same kind.\n- **Bottom storey:** a drawer (drawer:0#0,0#cut) sits on the cut face of the bottom half base.\n- **Top storey:** an open bin with three compartments and no lid (hex-bin-half-n-full-div3).\n- **Middle storey:** empty. It's a plain storey and its cut face is left open.\n\nI capped the open faces and bolted the joints. The configurator check found no rule errors and the parts don't collide. The build is 25 parts.",
    "outcome": "built"
